## Problem

# OKRs are freetext prose in AGENTS.md True Grit section:
# - Not queryable by `b00t datums list --type=okr`
# - Not linkable from `b00t task`
# - Not automatable: sm0l agents cannot update KR status
# - Re-emitted in full on every `b00t whoami` call — wasteful

## Finished State

# `b00t datums list --type=okr` returns all active OKRs.
# `b00t task add "foo" --okr=<datum-name>` links task to KR.
# sm0l agents can `b00t datum update <name> okr.kr[0].status=pass` without frontier involvement.
# `b00t hive run` checks `okr.status != blocked` before resource-heavy ops.

## Schema

# ```toml
# [b00t]
# name = "okr-<slug>"
# type = "okr"
# hint = "one sentence objective"

# [okr]
# objective = "one sentence system outcome"
# owner = "agent-pid-or-role"
# quarter = "2026-Q3"
# status = "active"  # active|blocked|complete|cancelled

# [[okr.kr]]
# id = "kr1"
# description = "human-readable check"
# check = "cargo test -p b00t-cli 2>&1 | tail -1"
# pass_pattern = "test result: ok"
# owner = "sm0l"
# tier = "sm0l"
# status = "pending"  # pending|pass|fail|blocked
# task_ids = []
# ```

## Acceptance Criteria

# - [ ] `_b00t_/datums/OKR.tomllmd` schema datum written and stable
# - [ ] `b00t datum list --type=okr` returns OKR datums
# - [ ] `b00t task add <title> --okr=<name>` links task to KR (append task_id)
# - [ ] sm0l agent can set `okr.kr[n].status` via `b00t datum update`
# - [ ] At least one live OKR instance datum created for current hive goal

## Sub-tasks

